  "id": "COMPOUND:296 - PROTEIN:897",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a relationship between talbutal and Gamma-aminobutyric acid receptor subunit alpha-3, as all three paths point to a common mechanism: talbutal targets the same subunit as ganaxolone, zopiclone, and carisoprodol. This indicates that talbutal may act through a shared molecular pathway that influences the activity of the gamma-aminobutyric acid (GABA) receptor subunit alpha-3. The high scores in all three paths suggest that the target relationship is well-supported, with talbutal potentially acting as a GABA receptor modulator. The consistency across different drugs that target the same subunit implies that talbutal may exert its effects by interacting with this receptor subunit, possibly through a common mechanism that is not yet fully understood. The integration of these paths highlights the role of the GABA receptor subunit alpha-3 in the pharmacological action of talbutal, though further investigation is needed to clarify the exact mechanism of interaction.",
